    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0261" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/938</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-15">October 15, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Welles</hi>: Mr. Hornbeck and I, upon giving
                    further consideration to the matter, are of the opinion that if Mr. Browder is
                    to give out and publish the other statement which you gave him<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d197-f1"/> it would be well for Mr. Browder to publish this
                        statement<anchor n="55" xml:id="d197-f2"/> also.</p>
                <p>(If this statement is to be sent to him, the first page would need to be retyped
                    in as much as it bears the FE date stamp.)<anchor n="56" xml:id="d197-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="54" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>See statement of October 12, <ref target="#pg248">p. 248</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f2" n="55" xml:id="d197-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f3" n="56" xml:id="d197-f3-content">
                <p>In reply to an inquiry dated May 19, 1950, Mr. Hamilton wrote on May 26: “I have
                    no recollection of having had any knowledge regarding the occasion of Mr.
                    Browder’s call or of the statement handed to Mr. Browder by Mr. Welles until
                    after Mr. Browder had called and had been given the statement” (893.01/938).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
